 "result": "I read all 20 modules in full, in order. In each one, the only function that divides is its `share_nXX(total, parts)` helper, which returns `total / parts`. None of the hundreds of `step_*` functions divide; they only multiply, add, compare and take square roots.\n\n**Functions that divide without checking for zero first (5):**\n\n| Module | Function |\n|---|---|\n| `calc/n02.py` | `share_n02` (`calc/n02.py:5`) |\n| `calc/n07.py` | `share_n07` (`calc/n07.py:5`) |\n| `calc/n11.py` | `share_n11` (`calc/n11.py:5`) |\n| `calc/n15.py` | `share_n15` (`calc/n15.py:5`) |\n| `calc/n19.py` | `share_n19` (`calc/n19.py:5`) |\n\nEach of these raises `ZeroDivisionError` when `parts == 0`. The other 15 `share_*` functions check `if parts == 0: return 0` before dividing.\n\n**Answers:**\n\n- **(a)** `MAX_BATCH = 384` (`calc/n04.py:9`).\n- **(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in `calc/n13.py` (`calc/n13.py:9`). It returns `min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n- **(c)** In `calc/n17.py`, `close_books(rows)` calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`).\n\nOne small oddity: each file's docstring names a different module than its filename. For example, `n01.py` says \"calc.m21\" and `n20.py` says \"calc.m40\". It doesn't affect any of the answers.",
